1
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:11,310
Over a century ago, beings that
prey on humans suddenly appeared.

2
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:21,190
Their absolutely overwhelming strength

3
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,240
quickly pushed humanity to
the brink of extinction.

4
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:36,330
The surviving humans constructed
three walls: Maria, Rose, and Sina,

5
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:39,880
which brought them a century of peace.

6
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,500
However...

7
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:03,150
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

8
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:08,610
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

9
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:13,700
Prayers won't solve anything

10
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:19,040
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

11
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:24,340
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

12
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:26,880
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

13
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:29,760
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

14
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:35,140
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

15
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:40,440
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

16
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:45,650
consumed with surging bloodlust,

17
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:52,780
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

18
00:02:14,989 --> 00:02:19,994
That Day: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 2

19
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:41,250
Till that time I had been a wretched soul,
and wholly giv'n to greed!

20
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:48,130
Now, as thou see'st,
I'm punished for it here!

21
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:51,720
What avarice doth

22
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:57,220
is here made manifest,
in this purgation of converted souls!

23
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:05,350
Nor hath this Mount a penalty more bitter!

24
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,120
Stop!

25
00:03:20,330 --> 00:03:21,620
Let me go!

26
00:03:21,830 --> 00:03:24,420
O Avarice!

27
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:28,040
Thou hast to thyself so drawn my race,

28
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:33,220
that ev'n for its own flesh it careth not!

29
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:36,970
What more canst thou do with us?!

30
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:44,600
O Avarice! Thou hast to thyself...

31
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,780
Eren! What are you doing?!

32
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:02,790
We were so close to saving Mom!

33
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Why couldn't you mind your own business?!

34
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:09,420
- We were so close to saving her!
- Knock it off, dammit!

35
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,460
Eren!

36
00:04:16,550 --> 00:04:17,970
Eren.

37
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:23,850
You couldn't save your mother

38
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:26,230
because you lacked the strength.

39
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,690
And I...

40
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:35,900
I couldn't stand up to the Titan...

41
00:04:36,110 --> 00:04:39,030
...because I lacked the courage!

42
00:04:49,710 --> 00:04:51,340
I'm sorry.

43
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:04,680
It's happened again...

44
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:22,280
Hurry! To the inner gate!

45
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:26,330
Escape aboard the boats there!

46
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:30,670
Hurry! Before you get eaten!

47
00:05:43,350 --> 00:05:47,930
City districts like Shiganshina that
stick out in vital spots along the wall

48
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:55,070
serve to attract the Titans and streamline
security costs and troop numbers.

49
00:05:55,270 --> 00:05:58,650
Performing true to its role as a Titan target,

50
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:05,530
Shiganshina had but one inner gate
through which its citizens could flee.

51
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:10,120
Discard your belongings!

52
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:12,960
Let as many people on as possible!

53
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:19,420
Sit, Armin.

54
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:23,680
But Eren and Mikasa still aren't here.

55
00:06:23,890 --> 00:06:25,720
There they are!

56
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,020
Eren?

57
00:06:30,850 --> 00:06:33,560
Just let him be for now.

58
00:06:33,770 --> 00:06:37,230
The poor thing.
How very traumatized he must be...

59
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,860
Huh?

60
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:43,410
What are you dawdling for?!
Hurry the hell up!

61
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:45,570
Get those cannons loaded!

62
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,250
Hurry!

63
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,380
They're closing in!

64
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:13,560
This can't be for real...!

65
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:17,270
Please, God...
Please, God... Please, God...

66
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:19,110
Hey!

67
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,490
Hey! What are you doing?!

68
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:23,780
It's at full capacity! It has to leave!

69
00:07:23,990 --> 00:07:27,320
No! Please! At least let our children on!

70
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,240
I'm sorry, but we can't!

71
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:31,080
Get going!

72
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:36,170
- Let us on!
- Let us on!

73
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,980
You idiot! What are you aiming at?!

74
00:07:55,190 --> 00:07:59,310
B-But, Sir, these aren't
accurate enough to aim with!

75
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:03,780
I don't give a crap!
Get 'em reloaded at once!

76
00:08:03,990 --> 00:08:05,490
It's no use!

77
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,870
The gate's closing...!

78
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,290
Retreat! We're gonna get left behind!

79
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,920
Hey!

80
00:08:18,250 --> 00:08:20,710
Don't shut it! Hold on a little longer!

81
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:23,510
There are still lots of people in there!

82
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:25,510
If the Titans get through,

83
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:29,050
the town being overrun
will be the least of our worries!

84
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:32,970
All of humankind will be forced
to withdraw behind the next wall!

85
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:37,850
But that's no reason to
leave these people to die!

86
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:38,900
Shut it! Hurry!

87
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:40,650
The Titans are coming!

88
00:08:41,570 --> 00:08:43,610
Close the gate at once!

89
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,740
Stop!

90
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:49,700
Hey!

91
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:29,240
What the...?

92
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,450
It's...!

93
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:34,080
Fire!

94
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:43,960
- What?!
- No effect?!

95
00:09:46,630 --> 00:09:48,050
It's...!

96
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:53,010
It's coming! Retreat!

97
00:09:53,220 --> 00:09:56,060
A Titan's coming! It's charging this way!

98
00:09:56,270 --> 00:09:59,100
Hurry! Shut the gate!

99
00:10:33,930 --> 00:10:35,550
The gate...

100
00:11:04,210 --> 00:11:09,210
Within hours of the fall of Shiganshina
on the south side of Wall Maria,

101
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:15,800
news of the incident had reached
every city inside human territory.

102
00:11:16,010 --> 00:11:20,680
Is it true the Titans
have overrun Shiganshina?!

103
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:22,310
I can't believe this!

104
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:25,480
The walls have held strong
for a century! Why now?!

105
00:11:25,690 --> 00:11:27,560
Whether we believe it or not,

106
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:30,780
the fact is that refugees have
fled here by boat!

107
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:33,780
Reports say there are five hundred on board.

108
00:11:33,990 --> 00:11:37,780
The question is if Shiganshina
is all that was affected...

109
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:43,330
But, surely they couldn't have
gotten through Wall Maria as well?

110
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,130
In any event,

111
00:11:47,330 --> 00:11:49,670
we must contact the central
government and request instructions.

112
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:54,880
This crisis is far too much
for us to handle on our own.

113
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,590
I'm sorry to interrupt!

114
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,680
A courier horse has just arrived!

115
00:11:58,890 --> 00:12:03,520
Titans have breached
Wall Maria and entered its interior!

116
00:12:11,070 --> 00:12:12,690
It's over...

117
00:12:14,030 --> 00:12:16,070
It's all over...

118
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:20,410
The Titans are going
to devour humanity again...

119
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,290
This is the end...?

120
00:12:23,830 --> 00:12:29,540
I'll... never see
that house... ever again...

121
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:33,760
Why...?!

122
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:38,970
Why'd I argue for no reason like that?!
Why was that all I could do?!

123
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:41,390
And now Mom's gone!

124
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,850
She's never coming back!

125
00:12:46,810 --> 00:12:48,940
Why...?!

126
00:12:49,150 --> 00:12:52,650
Because you lacked the strength.

127
00:12:54,650 --> 00:12:58,240
It's because I'm weak...
Because humans are weak...

128
00:12:58,450 --> 00:13:01,910
ls crying the only
thing the weak can do?!

129
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:19,220
I'm... going to...

130
00:13:19,430 --> 00:13:20,260
Eren.

131
00:13:20,470 --> 00:13:22,430
What's gotten into you, Eren?

132
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:24,810
Eren...

133
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:27,680
...drive them out!

134
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:31,150
I'm going to drive out...

135
00:13:31,350 --> 00:13:34,230
...every last one from this world!

136
00:13:35,030 --> 00:13:36,440
Eren...

137
00:13:42,410 --> 00:13:46,540
The same year, the central
government made the decision

138
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:50,620
to withdraw all of humanity's
domain behind Wall Rose.

139
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:56,380
An estimated 10,000 people
were eaten by Titans during this time.

140
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:58,970
Eren...

141
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:00,180
Carla...

142
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:01,890
Mikasa...

143
00:14:02,090 --> 00:14:04,100
Please be all right!

144
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:08,020
Eren!

145
00:14:08,770 --> 00:14:09,770
Eren!

146
00:14:10,310 --> 00:14:11,310
Eren!

147
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:13,150
Eren!

148
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,150
Dad!

149
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:15,770
Stop, Dad!

150
00:14:17,030 --> 00:14:19,110
What are you trying to do?!

151
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,700
Just give me your arm!

152
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,200
No!

153
00:14:22,410 --> 00:14:25,080
Mom's death has made you go crazy!

154
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:26,120
Eren!

155
00:14:26,330 --> 00:14:28,620
Let go, Dad!

156
00:14:28,830 --> 00:14:29,830
It's for...

157
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:30,910
...your own sake!

158
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,540
What are you talking about?!

159
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:35,380
Listen! Don't forget the key!

160
00:14:35,590 --> 00:14:38,090
You must reach it!

161
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:42,300
Until... you learn...
the truth someday...!

162
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:52,850
Eren. Are you okay?

163
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:54,900
You were having a nightmare.

164
00:14:55,810 --> 00:14:58,900
I feel like I just saw Dad...

165
00:14:59,110 --> 00:15:01,740
No. You were dreaming.

166
00:15:02,650 --> 00:15:04,070
Oh...

167
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:09,700
Let's go.

168
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:12,660
They said they're going to hand out food.

169
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:20,630
Apparently this was their food storehouse.

170
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:24,760
They've gathered all the boat refugees here.

171
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:37,560
- Hey! Get in line, will ya?!
- Shut up!

172
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:40,730
I ain't eaten anything since last night!

173
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:44,740
We can't say we've survived just yet.

174
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:45,740
Eren!

175
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:47,370
Mikasa!

176
00:15:47,570 --> 00:15:48,990
Armin...

177
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:52,370
Here! Just in time!

178
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:56,290
My grandpa got us some
by saying it was for children!

179
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:58,130
Thank you.

180
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:05,630
What's his problem?

181
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,300
You can't blame him.

182
00:16:07,510 --> 00:16:10,680
There's probably not
enough food to go around.

183
00:16:10,890 --> 00:16:13,220
And that's an entire day's worth.

184
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:15,270
There are just too many refugees.

185
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,440
There was already
a food shortage going on,

186
00:16:17,650 --> 00:16:20,980
plus the people here aren't treated
as well as citizens on the outer wall.

187
00:16:21,190 --> 00:16:22,320
- This is mine!
- Shut up!

188
00:16:22,530 --> 00:16:25,990
Why should we hafta give our
food to some lousy outsiders?

189
00:16:26,990 --> 00:16:29,320
If the Titans got through the wall,

190
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:32,990
they could've at least eaten
some more people, if you ask me!

191
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,290
Eren!

192
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:41,250
This is just gonna make
the food shortage even worse.

193
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:42,880
Oww!

194
00:16:43,710 --> 00:16:46,630
What the hell?! You damn kid!

195
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:50,680
You don't know what it's like!

196
00:16:50,890 --> 00:16:53,180
You've never even seen it!

197
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:58,100
You've never seen
what the Titans do to people!

198
00:16:59,150 --> 00:16:59,940
Shut up!

199
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:01,270
I apologize!

200
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:03,940
He's just hungry and irritable!

201
00:17:04,150 --> 00:17:07,860
That's why he so rudely
lashed out at an adult...

202
00:17:08,070 --> 00:17:11,370
I'm very sorry!

203
00:17:13,870 --> 00:17:14,990
Man...

204
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:20,330
It's 'cause of us that you guys
aren't starving to death, you know!

205
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:23,750
Even you kids oughta be thankful to us!

206
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:25,340
Of course!

207
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:26,970
Damn...

208
00:17:27,170 --> 00:17:30,510
I refuse to let them take care of me.

209
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:34,810
I'm going back. To Wall Maria!

210
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:37,730
I'm going to destroy every last Titan!

211
00:17:37,930 --> 00:17:38,850
Eren...

212
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:41,100
You're not being serious, are you?

213
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:42,860
I'm serious!

214
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:46,860
I'm not like those guys who do
nothing but act tough inside the walls!

215
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:49,780
I don't need this crap!

216
00:17:51,410 --> 00:17:53,530
Eren! You'll starve to death!

217
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,790
Doesn't it bother you at all?!

218
00:17:55,990 --> 00:17:58,870
It's because we take everyone's
charity that we can't beat the Titans!

219
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:01,290
It's impossible!
There is no beating them!

220
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:04,170
All we can do is live inside the walls!

221
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:07,340
If we try anything, we'll die!
Just like my mom and dad!

222
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:11,090
So you're just gonna grovel to them then?!
That's not shameful to you?!

223
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,470
There's... There's nothing
we can do for now!

224
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,310
That's just an excuse!

225
00:18:15,510 --> 00:18:18,600
If you wanna live like
livestock forever, go ahead!

226
00:18:18,810 --> 00:18:20,640
You wimp!

227
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:25,770
Mikasa...

228
00:18:34,490 --> 00:18:38,290
If Armin's a wimp, then so are we.

229
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:42,210
Whether it was running
from the Titans or fleeing the town,

230
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:46,000
we didn't manage anything on our own.

231
00:18:46,210 --> 00:18:49,050
We even had help finding food today.

232
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:51,470
There's no way such powerless people

233
00:18:51,670 --> 00:18:55,180
can defeat even a
single one of those Titans.

234
00:18:56,350 --> 00:18:59,180
Staying alive is what matters most.

235
00:18:59,390 --> 00:19:01,640
Just like your mother said.

236
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,650
Mikasa!

237
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:11,610
You have to eat and stay alive.

238
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:14,570
I won't let you starve to death.

239
00:19:25,630 --> 00:19:28,800
Several days later,
the throngs of refugees

240
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,590
were tasked with cultivating
the wastelands to secure food.

241
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:38,350
However, a food shortage was unavoidable.

242
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,770
So, in the following year of 846,

243
00:19:40,970 --> 00:19:44,020
the central government sent a
multitude of refugees on a mission

244
00:19:44,230 --> 00:19:47,810
in the name of retaking Wall Maria.

245
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:59,280
Of the 250,000 sent...

246
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:01,790
nearly 20% of the population...

247
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,750
not even 200 survived.

248
00:20:06,540 --> 00:20:09,500
Although it wasn't much,
their sacrifices did improve

249
00:20:09,710 --> 00:20:14,050
the food shortage situation
for the rest of the population.

250
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:29,310
It's all the Titans' fault.

251
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:32,730
If we could just subdue them,

252
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:36,780
our place in the world could be ours again.

253
00:20:38,030 --> 00:20:39,740
Armin.

254
00:20:39,950 --> 00:20:42,950
I'm going to apply for the Cadets next year.

255
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:48,880
I'm going to gain the
strength to fight the Titans!

256
00:20:52,250 --> 00:20:53,210
Me too...

257
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:54,420
Armin?!

258
00:20:54,630 --> 00:20:56,050
Me too!

259
00:20:57,090 --> 00:20:58,590
I will, too.

260
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,720
Mikasa...!

261
00:20:59,930 --> 00:21:04,270
You don't need to! You said yourself
staying alive is what's important!

262
00:21:04,470 --> 00:21:09,310
Yes. That's why I'm doing it;
so you won't die.

263
00:21:13,020 --> 00:21:16,320
All right. The three of us, then.

264
00:21:23,330 --> 00:21:28,540
The 104th Cadet Corps Class
entrance ceremony will now begin!

265
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:33,630
You have the misfortune of having me,
Keith Sadies, as your commandant!

266
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:36,300
I do not welcome you warmly!

267
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:39,590
In your current state, you'd
be nothing but food for the Titans!

268
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:43,220
You're mere livestock!
You're less than livestock!

269
00:21:43,430 --> 00:21:48,810
Over the next three years,
we're going to train you worthless nothings

270
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:51,810
and teach you how to fight Titans!

271
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:55,440
Three years from now, when you
come face-to-face with the Titans,

272
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:57,490
will you still be fodder for them?!

273
00:21:57,690 --> 00:22:01,200
Will you serve as an honorable
barrier that protects the king?!

274
00:22:01,410 --> 00:22:05,540
Or will you be a glorious soldier
for humanity that drives the Titans out!

275
00:22:05,740 --> 00:22:07,450
It's up to you to decide!

276
00:22:08,790 --> 00:22:11,580
Yes. I'll be one.

277
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:16,630
I'll drive out every last Titan!

278
00:22:39,570 --> 00:22:44,280
Your dreams are where your heart is

279
00:22:44,490 --> 00:22:50,540
They're more fragile than life itself

280
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:55,250
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

281
00:22:55,460 --> 00:23:01,970
Now, rest in peace

282
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:13,060
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

283
00:23:13,270 --> 00:23:23,570
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

284
00:23:23,780 --> 00:23:29,540
In this beautiful, cruel world

285
00:23:29,740 --> 00:23:34,830
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

286
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:40,460
Oh, with our strength- and our weakness...

287
00:23:40,670 --> 00:23:46,010
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

288
00:23:46,220 --> 00:23:50,810
to anything anymore?

289
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:58,900
He fails as a soldier.

290
00:23:59,110 --> 00:24:03,400
Eren joins the Cadets,
vowing revenge against the Titans,

291
00:24:03,610 --> 00:24:07,509
but his failure at basic training
comes as a harsh reality.

292
00:24:07,509 --> 00:24:09,700
A Dim Light Amid Despair: Humanity's Comeback, Part 1
but his failure at basic training
comes as a harsh reality.

293
